From 907dfd5ddef8d718f54453da6d0c4b574a52975b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kamil Monicz <kamil@monicz.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:02:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 90/93] fdt: ddtprune: don't prune every unique entry for a
 target below one entry

A percentage prune rounds its target down to whole entries.  When the
target is zero, for example 1% of a table with fewer than 100 unique
entries, the search for the oldest age bin to keep never runs, the
cutoff stays at the current time, and the walk prunes every unique
entry instead of none.

Return without pruning when the target is zero.

Ported from openzfs/zfs#19264 (7391add).

Signed-off-by: Kamil Monicz <kamil@monicz.dev>
---
 usr/src/uts/common/fs/zfs/ddt.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/usr/src/uts/common/fs/zfs/ddt.c b/usr/src/uts/common/fs/zfs/ddt.c
index 24754528..12840a34 100644
--- a/usr/src/uts/common/fs/zfs/ddt.c
+++ b/usr/src/uts/common/fs/zfs/ddt.c
@@ -2852,6 +2852,8 @@ ddt_prune_unique_entries(spa_t *spa, zpool_ddt_prune_unit_t unit,
 		ddt_prune_walk(spa, 0, &histogram);
 
 		uint64_t target = (histogram.dah_entries * amount) / 100;
+		if (target == 0)
+			goto out;
 
 		/*
 		 * Figure out our cutoff date (i.e., which bins to prune from).
-- 
